"""Small front page, full evidence available without hiding failed alternatives."""
from html import escape
from .review import *
from .evaluate import METHODS
CAPTIONS={
'P1':'User: J better, S acceptable. M/B retain S’s 540px; no claimed improvement over preferred J. C expands the lower lobe. No thickness pruning.',
'P2':'User: J poor, S good. M/A/B/C preserve all 495 S pixels exactly. Dim diffuse red survives beside the bright peak; J keeps only 200px.',
'P3':'User: J better, S slightly worse. M/B equal S (446px), so the preferred J boundary remains an unresolved advantage. C adds a tail/notch rather than solving it.',
'P4':'User: J bad, S acceptable. M/B retain S’s 320px and separate the visible neighbors. Edge case: secondary priority; no central tradeoff was made.',
'P5':'User: J acceptable, S merges yellows. Two real intensity maxima lost their markers at a single-pixel hue gate. M/B recover them, reduce 1817→664px and separate the target. A gives 665px; C leaves 777px and residual lobes.',
'C01':'Central red: all M/B anchor pixels equal S; J truncates diffuse material. Weak fresh cue elsewhere in this crop still exceeds the area ceiling.',
'C02':'Central red anchor remains577px in M/B. C grows806px. A separate weak interstice cue merges neighbors in M/S; B reduces it to131px but is illumination-sensitive. Do not certify that tinted highlight as a red bead.',
'C03':'Central yellow anchor remains596px in M/B. A extends a thin route toward the lower-left yellow; C adds neighboring material. B’s separate92px edge/interstice proposal remains color/identity uncertain.',
'C04':'Central yellow group remains photographically separated at the anchor. A weak fresh885px cue still includes both sides of a dark-profile pair and is flagged. Marker repair is not a complete merger solution.',
'C05':'Strong-highlight red: M/B preserve527px, J248px. A1134px reaches neighboring reds and is rejected; C742px leaves spurious extensions. Central failure counts against A/C.',
'C06':'Same-color central pair: M/B preserve441px anchor and neighboring interiors. Multiple cues still duplicate one proposal; a1086px nearby support is flagged.',
'C07':'Opposite-side selection: M/B preserve384px anchor. Four near proposals collapse to two overlap groups; do not report four recovered beads. Compact-support side can change as supported material grows.',
'C08':'Additional central yellow: M/B preserve470px anchor. Fresh weak red cue expands1129px into uncertain shaded material and is flagged, not counted as new recovery.',
'C09':'Secondary clear-edge red: M/B preserve319px; difficult surrounding edge material need not be resolved. No tuning on this edge example.',
'C10':'Secondary clear-edge yellow: M/B preserve437px. A594px is domain/illumination-sensitive. Nearby red995px remains flagged; no central quality tradeoff to rescue it.'}

def table(o):
    head='<table><tr><th>Method</th><th>Native px</th><th>+ / − vs S</th><th>Centroid ΔS</th><th>Boundary ∇Y</th><th>Geometry / status</th></tr>'
    for m,r in o['variants'].items():
        t=r['metrics'];head+=f'<tr><td>{m}</td><td>{t["area"]}</td><td>+{t["added"]} / −{t["removed"]}</td><td>{(t["centroid_shift"] or 0):.2f}px</td><td>{(t["boundary_gradient"] or 0):.4f}</td><td>{r["centerline"]["side"]}; '+escape(', '.join(r['abstention_reasons']) or 'unrated')+'</td></tr>'
    return head+'</table>'
def img(name,alt):return f'<a href="{name}.png"><img loading="lazy" src="{name}.png" alt="{escape(alt)}"></a>'
def main():
    dev=read(OUT/'development.json.gz')['cases'];conf=read(OUT/'confirmation.json.gz')['cases'];ev=read(OUT/'evaluation.json');html=['''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>R286 dark boundaries</title><style>body{font:17px/1.5 system-ui,sans-serif;max-width:1350px;margin:auto;padding:24px;background:#f6f5f1;color:#242424}h1,h2{line-height:1.2}section{background:white;padding:20px;margin:20px 0;border:1px solid #ddd;border-radius:8px}img{width:100%;height:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;display:block;overflow:auto;font-size:14px}td,th{padding:7px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;text-align:left}details{margin:15px 0}summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:600}a{color:#064e84}.note{background:#fff2cf;padding:12px}.native{image-rendering:pixelated;max-width:194px}</style><h1>R286 — stop at photographed dark separations</h1><p><strong>Preferred change for review: M, context-supported marker repair.</strong> It fixes the demonstrated P5 marker loss while preserving P2 exactly. B adds protected watershed interfaces, but can falsely split internal shading. A and C fail on independent central cases. Nothing is adopted into production.</p><p>Start with P5 and P2, then the independent failures. White + is a photographic centroid, never a physical bead center. Red barrier pixels are diagnostics; cyan fills are exact native support. Counts below are proposals, not verified beads.</p><p><a href="../../R286_REPORT.md">Report</a> · <a href="../../R286_P5_DIAGNOSIS.md">Root-cause diagnosis</a> · <a href="../../R286_REPRODUCE.md">Reproduction</a> · <a href="../../R286_CHECKLIST.md">Requirements</a> · <a href="../../r286/results/evaluation.json">Full numerical evidence</a></p>''']
    html.append('<section id="diagnosis"><h2>Why S crossed P5</h2><p>The two neighboring bright maxima were slightly outside a one-pixel hue gate. Their surrounding material was valid, but their markers vanished. All three regions therefore belonged to one watershed basin before merging. Brighter detours bypassed the direct dark valleys. Restoring context-supported markers fixes this demonstrated cause; lowering a saddle threshold alone would not.</p>'+img('P5-root-cause','P5 exact intensity, markers, paths and domain diagnosis')+'</section>')
    for case in [dev[4],dev[1],dev[0],dev[2],dev[3]]:
        name=case['name'];o=case['observations'][0];html.append(f'<section id="{name}"><h2>{name} — reviewed development</h2><p>{CAPTIONS[name]}</p>'+img(name+'-choice',name+' original J S and B; M equals B here')+'<p>M and B are identical in all five reviewed cases. The compact strip labels B; the full comparison shows every method.</p>'+f'<details><summary>All methods, exact fills, brightness profiles and numbers</summary>{img(name+"-all",name+" all six methods")}{table(o)}<a href="{name}-native.png">Exact native97 crop</a></details></section>')
    html.append('<section id="two-sided"><h2>All three original two-sided observations</h2>'+img('two-sided-three','Lower yellow, left red and right yellow preserved separately')+'<p>All three remain separate photographic observations. The right yellow is a supplementary previously reviewed control, not an independent confirmation case.</p><details><summary>Right yellow native evidence</summary>'+img('P1-right-yellow-all','Right yellow all methods')+'<a href="two-sided-native.png">Native131 group</a> · <a href="P1-right-yellow-native.png">Native97 right yellow</a></details></section>')
    html.append('<section id="confirmation"><h2>Frozen independent confirmation</h2><p>Ten regions selected before new outputs: eight central, two clear-edge. All52 nearby cues survive, including weak and fresh cues. M/B preserve all10 selected anchor supports exactly. Unrated does not mean accepted. J/S lack the new full perturbation protocol, so their apparent flag counts are not comparable.</p><table><tr><th>Candidate</th><th>Flagged /52</th><th>Domain-sensitive</th><th>Illumination-sensitive</th><th>Mean ΔS</th><th>Near central proposals*</th></tr>')
    for m in ('M','A','B','C'):
        r=ev['confirmation_all'][m];html.append(f'<tr><td>{m}</td><td>{r["flagged"]}/52</td><td>{r["domain_sensitive"]}</td><td>{r["illumination_sensitive"]}</td><td>{r["mean_centroid_shift_from_S"]:.2f}px</td><td>{ev["central"][m]["reviewable_near"]}</td></tr>')
    html.append('</table><p>*Unflagged support-near observations before deduplication, not physical beads. M/B:29 central near proposals form25 overlap groups across eight crops; weak ownership remains unresolved. Eight fresh cues include three flagged supports and five overlapping old proposals; no new distinct bead is established.</p></section>')
    for case in conf:
        name=case['name'];o=min(case['observations'],key=lambda o:np.linalg.norm(np.array(o['seed'])-case['seed']));html.append(f'<section id="{name}"><h2>{name} — {escape(case["stratum"])}</h2><p>{CAPTIONS[name]}</p>'+img(name+'-group',name+' all nearby cues')+'<details><summary>Anchor alternatives, all-cue atlas, profiles and native crops</summary>'+img(name+'-all',name+' anchor alternatives')+table(o)+img(name+'-atlas',name+' every cue including failures')+f'<a href="{name}-native.png">Native97 anchor</a> · <a href="{name}-group-native.png">Native161 group</a></details></section>')
    for q in read(OUT/'additional-review.json'):
        html.append('<section id="'+q['name']+'"><h2>Preserved weak-cue difference: '+q['case']+'</h2><p>'+escape(CAPTIONS[q['case']])+'</p>'+img(q['name']+'-all','Protected watershed weak-cue difference')+f'<a href="{q["name"]}-native.png">Exact native crop</a></section>')
    html.append('<section id="mechanisms"><h2>Shading counterexample — stronger protection can fail</h2><p>B splits the shallow-shading control; M preserves it. All methods separate the deep valley, but identical pixels could be deep texture on one body. That ownership ambiguity cannot be solved by shape or a brightness threshold alone.</p>'+img('mechanisms','Shading and seam controls, including false split')+'</section>')
    syn=read(OUT/'synthetic-summary.json')['totals'];html.append('<section id="synthetic"><h2>Fresh physical rendering controls — limited transfer</h2><p>Four certified noninterpenetrating POV scenes,41 automatic colored cues. Identity rasters opened only after saved inference. Purity ≥95% is synthetic evaluation, not real-photo calibration. These results remain poor and do not establish general reliable ownership.</p><table><tr><th>Method</th><th>Within870</th><th>Pure / eligible proposals</th><th>Distinct recovered /74</th><th>Duplicate pure proposals</th></tr>')
    for m,r in syn.items():html.append(f'<tr><td>{m}</td><td>{r["within_cap"]}</td><td>{r["pure"]}/{r["within_cap"]}</td><td>{r["recovered"]}/74</td><td>{r["duplicates"]}</td></tr>')
    html.append('</table><details><summary>All four rendered scenes and inferred supports</summary>')
    for i in range(4):
        folder=OUT/'synthetic'/f'scene-{i:02}';im=np.asarray(Image.open(folder/'analysis-srgb.png'));obs=read(folder/'inference.json.gz');fig,axs=plt.subplots(1,7,figsize=(19,3.4))
        for ax,m in zip(axs,['raw']+list(METHODS)):
            ax.imshow(im);ax.set_title(m);ax.set_xticks([]);ax.set_yticks([])
            if m=='raw':continue
            for o in obs:
                pts=pixels(o['supports'][m]);mask=np.zeros(im.shape[:2],bool);pts=pts[np.all((pts>=0)&(pts<[320,224]),axis=1)]
                if len(pts):mask[pts[:,1],pts[:,0]]=True;ax.contour(mask,levels=[.5],colors=[COLORS[m]],linewidths=.5)
        fig.suptitle(f'Fresh physical scene{i}: all proposals, including failures');fig.tight_layout();fig.savefig(REVIEW/f'synthetic-{i:02}.png',dpi=110);plt.close(fig);html.append(img(f'synthetic-{i:02}','Rendered physical scene all methods'))
    html.append('</details></section>')
    black=read(OUT/'reflection-stability.json');html.append('<section id="P6"><h2>P6 — black specular reflections unchanged</h2><p>All144 native-mask / subpixel-contour / peak replays match R285 exactly (48 features × R1/R2/R4). Upper and lower supports overlap0px in each method. Retain R2, keep R1/R4 available. The lower feature remains a secondary reflection with unknown physical ownership.</p>')
    for q in black['selected']:html.append(img(q['name'],q['name']+' reflection-only alternatives')+f'<a href="{q["name"]}-native.png">Exact native49 crop</a>')
    html.append('</section><section id="decision"><h2>Recommendation and stopping point</h2><p>Prefer M’s context-supported marker repair for the next user-approved Phase1 direction. Keep B as an uncertain alternative; do not adopt its stronger protection globally after its shading failure. Retain J as a useful control for P1/P3. A/C are preserved failed candidates. Difficult edges need not be rescued.</p><p>No production inventory change, global fit or pattern search. Await user assessment of P5/P2 and independent failures before any next round.</p></section></html>')
    (REVIEW/'index.html').write_text('\n'.join(html))
if __name__=='__main__':main()
